{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"30ef3b2ff994cbe0","name":"card_event_last_ditch_force","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/OceaniaStorm/events/card_event_last_ditch_force","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LAST DITCH FORCE","text":"Destroy all units. Players lose 6 kredit slots. Units in decks get +3 attack.","flavorText":"By the summer of 1945, Japan was preparing a true last ditch defense of the Home Islands. Operation Ketsugō was designed to meet the expected Allied invasion with overwhelming resistance and inflict such heavy losses that the Allies might accept a negotiated end to the war. Japanese strategists correctly anticipated that southern Kyūshū would be the first major target and concentrated troops, aircraft and ammunition there. Hundreds of thousands of soldiers were deployed, while thousands of aircraft were prepared for kamikaze attacks against the invasion fleet. Midget submarines, manned torpedoes, suicide boats and specially trained divers were also ready to strike Allied ships approaching the beaches. The defense extended far beyond the regular armed forces. Millions of civilians were organized into the Volunteer Fighting Corps, often with little training and few modern weapons. Rifles, Molotov cocktails, swords and even bamboo spears were to be used in a final defense of Japanese territory. Operation Ketsugō was never carried out. Japan surrendered in August 1945 before the planned Allied invasion could begin.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":10,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_last_ditch_force","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_last_ditch_force_title","SourceString":"LAST DITCH FORCE","LocalizedString":"LAST DITCH FORCE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":10,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_last_ditch_force_text","SourceString":"Destroy all units. Players 